<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  dev.ailang.mission-recovery-motoko.plist — the motoko sibling of the v1 recovery job.

  mission-recovery.sh has been mission-parameterized since it was written (every path
  derives from MISSION_NAME — see its lines 32/42-47), but only ONE instance was ever
  installed and it is pinned to MISSION_NAME=v1. So motoko's .blocked marker had nothing
  watching it: measured 2026-08-14, ~/.ailang/state/mission-motoko.blocked sat untouched
  for 7+ hours while the recovery log showed an unbroken run of "mission v1 blocked" lines.

  Recovery matters MORE here than for v1, not less. mission-motoko's StartInterval is
  43200s (12h) against v1's 5400s (90m), so one refused fire costs a full half-day and
  the loop silently halves its own cadence.

  MEASURED REFUSAL RATE (re-derived at mission iteration 4, 2026-08-14 09:50, from
  /tmp/ailang-mission-motoko.log rather than transcribed): 6 refusals against 4 starts
  over the loop's whole life, i.e. 10 fires and a 60% refusal rate. Refusals at 08-12
  09:21, 08-13 00:25, 08-14 01:19, 08-14 08:57, 09:17, 09:37; starts at 08-12 10:32
  (iter 1), 08-12 11:37 (iter 2), 08-13 12:27 (iter 3), 08-14 09:45 (iter 4). The
  earlier draft of this comment said "three of six", which was correct when written at
  08:44 and is superseded by the three refusals that followed it.

  Only the FIRST refusal (08-12 09:19) carried a diagnostic — the Claude Code trust
  dialog, charter V22. Every refusal since reads `captured output: ''` on all three
  models across both attempts, which is a hang, not a quota message.

  The stall is TRANSIENT and FLEET-WIDE, not a motoko fault. Control, measured in the
  same window from /tmp/ailang-mission-control.log: v1 refused with the identical
  empty-output signature at 05:20, 05:36 and 08:49 on 08-14, overlapping motoko's
  08:47/09:07/09:27, and recovered each time — because its recovery job kickstarted it.
  Two independently-configured missions in two checkouts failing together is what makes
  this environmental rather than a per-mission defect.

  This job WORKS, and the evidence is not a smoke test: motoko iteration 4 exists only
  because of it. It kickstarted at 08:45, 09:05, 09:25 and 09:45; the first three
  re-probed and refused again, and the fourth got through. So the recovery model here is
  bounded brute retry against a stall that persisted ~1h — cheap enough to be the right
  answer, but note it treats the symptom. The empty-output probe hang itself is
  unexplained and is tracked as its own queue item.

  Cheap by construction, exactly as the v1 job: it does NOT call the API. It reads
  marker files and issues launchctl kickstart; the driver's own probes decide whether
  to proceed, and a failed retry spends zero tokens.

  Installation (the installed copy is a REGULAR FILE, not a symlink — editing this
  repo file changes nothing on the rig until you re-cp it):
    cp tools/launchd/dev.ailang.mission-recovery-motoko.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.ailang.mission-recovery-motoko.plist

  Kill switches (both survive reboots, no unload needed):
    touch ~/.ailang/state/mission-motoko.disabled    # motoko only — mission AND its recovery
    touch ~/.ailang/state/mission-recovery.disabled  # SHARED: silences v1 recovery too

  Note the second one is shared with the v1 job by design (the script's SELF_KILL_SWITCH
  is not namespaced). To stop only this loop, use the mission's own switch.

  Logs: /tmp/ailang-mission-recovery.log (shared with v1; lines carry the mission name)
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>dev.ailang.mission-recovery-motoko</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/voightkampff/dev/sunholo-data/ailang-motoko/tools/launchd/mission-recovery.sh</string>
    </array>

    <!-- 4 min, matching v1. The script is a few file stats unless the loop is blocked,
         so the poll is effectively free; the real pacing is the 20-min cooldown inside. -->
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>240</integer>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/Users/voightkampff/go/bin:/Users/voightkampff/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
        <key>MISSION_NAME</key>
        <string>motoko</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- Deliberately NOT RunAtLoad: a login/reboot should not immediately kickstart
         a mission iteration. The first poll happens 4 min in. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/ailang-mission-recovery-motoko.stdout</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/ailang-mission-recovery-motoko.stderr</string>
</dict>
</plist>
